# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Large / regenerated inputs and outputs. Nothing here belongs in git; every
# path below is either fetched by the pipeline or produced by it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reads are large and not yet deposited; only the documentation that describes
# them is tracked. Samplesheets and reference-set definitions live in assets/,
# which is tracked normally.
data/*
!data/readme.md
!data/reference_genomes.md

refs/
work/

# Pipeline outputs. Every analysis publishes under `results/`, including the
# secondary ones: results/q10 (quality-matched rerun) and results/raghavendra
# (prior-study reanalysis). One ignored path therefore covers all of them.
#
# `results_*/` is kept as a safety net, not because anything writes there now.
# Earlier revisions used --outdir results_q10 and --outdir results_raghavendra,
# so a stale command line or an old working copy can still produce those, and
# they hold GB. Ignoring the old shape costs nothing and stops a large
# accidental commit.
results/
results_*/
.nextflow/
.nextflow.log*

# Scratch and private material (manuscript prose lives in its own repo)
ignore/
manuscript/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
._*
*.swp

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Editor / language scratch
.Rhistory
.Rproj.user/

# Defensive: none of these exists in the repository today, and none should ever
# be committed. Listed so that a careless `git add -A` cannot introduce one.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa
id_ed25519
.netrc
_netrc
credentials.json
secrets.y*ml
*.xlsx
*.xls
